{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>Thus.</b> Creator of the heavens, for they have a line, which is a boundary for them:" "<b>and what stretches out from them.</b> Upon the earth, an allusion to the firmament:" "<b>who spreads out the earth and what springs from it.</b> A participle, and the qof is opened [with a kamatz gadol] because of the ayin, [like] הנוטע, 'he who plants' — 'does the ear not hear?' (Psalms 94:9):" "<b>and what springs from it.</b> These are the plants upon the face of the ground:" "<b>who gives breath.</b> To man, and they are the people who are upon it:" "<b>and spirit.</b> To the living creatures that walk:" "And he said <b>upon it</b> [upon man] because of his walking upright:"], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 42, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:32.541962014Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}